  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "progressive house: the four, a clap on two and four, a rolling offbeat bass and a sixteenth plucked arpeggio climbing the chord, under the long pad the style builds on",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "One bar: the arpeggio climbs root, third, fifth, octave and back in sixteenths on a short plucked keyboard; the bass plays the offbeat eighths with a ghost under each kick (a path cannot open on a rest); the pad is the composer's own. The long builds over 32 bars that define the style are the arrangement's, which a row cannot reach."
  }
